{"id": "EUVD-2026-96593", "enisaUuid": "21f905ef-1b15-3ba5-a427-e209b0c8e8de", "description": "JeecgBoot through 3.9.5 contains a missing authorization vulnerability in the OssFileController queryById handler that allows low-privileged authenticated users to read object storage file records. Attackers who know a record id can request GET /sys/oss/file/queryById to obtain original file names and direct storage URLs of files uploaded by other users.", "datePublished": "2026-10-10T21:49:41", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T12:40:39", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:L/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/AnkesKasty/cve-request-poc/blob/a7b6d1423555812d8efa26c91c5d0683164b31e5/JeecgBoot/poc_record_query_by_id.py", "https://github.com/jeecgboot/JeecgBoot/blob/e3b9dc0aefe1943d9772b026f64ed671a7c82802/jeecg-boot/jeecg-module-system/jeecg-system-biz/src/main/java/org/jeecg/modules/oss/controller/OssFileController.java#L84-L97", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/jeecgboot-through-3.9.5-missing-authorization-via-sys-oss-file-querybyid"], "aliases": ["GHSA-8fjj-r8xp-gq8v", "CVE-2026-108654"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.24, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "83f7e955-c3e3-3473-bdc4-03c4c0323023", "product": {"name": "JeecgBoot", "vendor": {"name": "n/a"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22643.9.5"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "4793ba47-27dc-3474-9865-305e9497ebf4", "vendor": {"name": "jeecgboot"}}], "isExploited": false}